<title>DUBAI: Saudi Arabia's Q1 M3 grows 4.7 pct qtr on qtr.</title>
<headline>Saudi Arabia's Q1 M3 grows 4.7 pct qtr on qtr.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's broadly defined M3 money supply grew 4.7 percent in the first quarter of 1997 over the previous quarter, Saudi Arabian Monetary Agency (SAMA) figures show.</p>
<p>Annual average M3 in 1996 grew 4.1 percent after expanding 3.5 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over three months)</p>
<p>			    Q1 1997		   Q4 1996</p>
<p>M3			   4.7			 1.8</p>
<p>M2			   5.9			 2.3</p>
<p>M1			   8.1			 0.6</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (riyal millions)</p>
<p>			    Q1 1997		   Q4 1996</p>
<p>M3			  264,788.4		 252,869.7</p>
<p>M2			  210,328.7		 198,549.0</p>
<p>M1			  140,346.2		 129,843.4</p>
</text>
